              "question": "Examine how the Vedāntic view and modern biology converge on the / concept of psycho-social evolution.",
              "solution_html": "<ul class=\"list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 my-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\"><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">In the modern age, there is a growing awareness of the need for personal</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">development, but often this is limited to the idea of individuality—focused on self</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">interest, external achievements, and personal success. However, the author of the</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">discussed passage, drawing from the insights of Vedānta and the teachings of Swami</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">Vivekananda, offers a deeper interpretation of human growth. He proposes that real</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">evolution lies in the transition from individuality to personality—a journey from ego</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">centered existence to spiritual fullness. This transition is not just psychological but</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">spiritual, and it forms an essential part of psycho-social evolution</li><li class=\"leading-relaxed text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">Essay Type questions. Answer 2 questions. Each question carries <span class=\"font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400\">(15 marks)</span> each.</li></ul>",
